    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Verification_Code</name>
        <label>Is there a verification record to link?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Record</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Has_Code</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>forB_HasVerificationCode</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Verification_Code_Case</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Link Case</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Called by the UC Assist Password Reset subagent. Redeems the one-time verification token (server re-check, US-3), finds the active portal user, resets the password, marks the verification Consumed, and logs a Case on every outcome (SUCCESS Closed; NOT_VERIFIED, NO_ACTIVE_USER, ERROR New in the Password Support queue). Runs in system mode because the Einstein agent user has no role and cannot see customer users through sharing. Update Message v1: first version, spec v1.0.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>forB_HasVerificationCode</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>NOT(ISBLANK({!varT_VerificationCodeId}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>forT_CaseOwnerId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!varT_Status} = 'SUCCESS', {!$User.Id}, {!Get_Password_Support_Queue.Id})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>forT_CaseStatus</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!varT_Status} = 'SUCCESS', 'Closed', 'New')</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>forT_CaseSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>'Agentforce password reset - ' &amp; {!varT_Status}</expression>
    </formulas>
